"value","2026-10-20","image","gameplay","The creator’s full theme-park screenshot, from the shared IsoCity/IsoCoaster repository.","src","/GameMap/assets/media/learning/isocoaster-cursor.webp","alt","An isometric theme park with intertwined colourful roller-coaster tracks, rides and paths.","https://github.com/amilich/isometric-city#readme","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","Creator-published screenshot","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)",[86],"Cursor","Creator evidence",[91],"evidence","section",{"_57":92,"_25":75,"_93":94},"Read the creator’s AI attribution","note","README distinguishes the two games, their hosts and separate local routes. Source-checked; full reproduction not performed.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[99],{"_57":100,"_25":101,"_93":102},"Open the complete game project","https://github.com/amilich/isometric-city","Complete IsoCity repository includes the dedicated src/app/coaster route, shared components and assets. npm install then npm run dev; open localhost:3000/coaster. MIT code; use a Node runtime compatible with its current Next 16 package.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[108],{"_57":109,"_25":110,"_93":111},"Play IsoCoaster","https://iso-coaster.com","Author-hosted browser theme-park builder; the shared source repository contains its separate coaster route.","Game platform","Browser","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[119],{"_57":120,"_25":75,"_93":-7},"Read the creator’s development disclosure","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[125,126,127,128],"Play the theme park builder and inspect how coaster tracks, rides and guests interact.","Run the repository locally and open /coaster rather than the city-building route.","Compare the coaster-specific state and interface with the shared isometric rendering components.","Ask an agent to adjust one ride or guest behavior, then test construction, simulation and save/load.","AI workflow / foundation context","The shared creator README attributes both games to Cursor. Study how a common isometric renderer supports a different simulation; the source does not disclose a specific model or a full AI conversation.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-assisted (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","2D","track","metadata","Engine","Custom Canvas 2D · TypeScript","engine","lead","2d","ai-assisted",[125,126,127,128],{"_57":120,"_25":75,"_17":115},{"_57":109,"_25":110,"_17":104,"_93":111},{"_57":100,"_25":101,"_93":102,"_154":155},{"_57":92,"_25":75,"_93":94},"resourceIds",[],"scope","complete-project",{"_157":158},"documents",{"_159":160,"_161":162},"en",[164,168,169,170,167,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,202,166,203,165,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220,221],"zh",[163,164,165,166,167],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-research","generative-api-boundaries","generation-delivery-contracts","asset-validation-contracts","asset-selection-feedback","visual-evidence-research","visual-feedback-mechanisms","game-development-evaluation","benchmark-reproducibility","gameplay-state-contracts","agent-interface-evidence","catalog-review-coverage","source-revision-notes","community-case-research","overview","catalog","contributing","media-sources","icon-sources","content-model","skills/level-design/SKILL","skills/level-design/LICENSE","skills/level-design/reference